vork on Debian, Ubuntu and Raspberry Pi OS
============================================

This is a prototype. The formats still change and the crypto awaits an
external review: keep nothing in it you can't lose.

What runs
---------
- vorkd, as a systemd user service in every user's session
  (`systemctl --user status vorkd`). Its store is ~/.local/share/vork.
- Reticulum: vorkd joins a shared instance on the machine, which this
  package doesn't bring: install any Reticulum implementation and run its
  shared instance. vorkd waits for it at start. Its connections are
  Reticulum's own, in its configuration file (~/.reticulum/config, read by
  every implementation), e.g. a TCP connection to a node you trust; the
  vork-desktop utility adds them there, or use your Reticulum's own tools.

First steps
-----------
    vork ping                 the daemon and this node's address
    vork heard                public libraries announced on the network
    vork library join NAME ADDRESS --lazy
    vork nodes                storage nodes heard
    (every library is a folder in ~/vork/NAME: vorkd mounts them itself)
    vork unmount NAME         takes one down until vorkd starts again

Optional services (systemctl --user enable --now ...):
    vork-gateway              libraries as websites at http://NAME.localhost:8740/
    vork-mount@NAME           a library mounted by systemd instead (vorkd --no-mounts)
    vork-extractd             attributes from files (see the unit for its token)

Settings: ~/.local/share/vork/vork.toml (the daemon writes a commented
one at first start). Headless machines: `sudo loginctl enable-linger USER`
keeps the user services running without a login.
